                <div class="postingContent">
                    <span id="lblSpecialRequirementText"><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">If mailing in an application, include <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="text-decoration-line: underline; color: #0000ff;">JC#452777</span></span></strong> on your State Application (STD678) in the &quot;Examination(s) or Job Title(s) for which you are applying&quot; section found under the “Questions” tab of your CalCareer application template. Applicants who do not submit the required information may not be considered for this job.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><strong><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Employment Application (STD.678):</span></strong></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">It is a requirement to submit work experience, dates, and hours worked, contact names and phone numbers of supervisors on the state application in order of current and old work experience. Resumes or other documents cannot substitute a state application. Applicants who fail to submit a completed STD.678 may not be considered. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">This position requires the applicant to be bilingual in ASL.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">A cover letter and resume are required and must be included.</span></div></span>
